{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1667","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Optimal Partition"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ integers. You should divide $$$a$$$ into continuous non-empty subarrays (there are $$$2^{n-1}$$$ ways to do that)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$s=a_l+a_{l+1}+\\ldots+a_r$$$. The value of a subarray $$$a_l, a_{l+1}, \\ldots, a_r$$$ is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(r-l+1)$$$ if $$$s \\gt 0$$$,"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$0$$$ if $$$s=0$$$,"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$-(r-l+1)$$$ if $$$s \\lt 0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" What is the maximum sum of values you can get with a partition?"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1$$$, $$$a_2$$$, ..., $$$a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$5 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case print a single integer — the maximum sum of values you can get with an optimal parition."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n3\n1 2 -3\n4\n0 -2 3 -4\n5\n-1 -2 3 -1 -1\n6\n-1 2 -3 4 -5 6\n7\n1 -1 -1 1 -1 -1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n2\n1\n6\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Test case $$$1$$$: one optimal partition is $$$[1, 2]$$$, $$$[-3]$$$. $$$1+2 \\gt 0$$$ so the value of $$$[1, 2]$$$ is $$$2$$$. $$$-3 \\lt 0$$$, so the value of $$$[-3]$$$ is $$$-1$$$. $$$2+(-1)=1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Test case $$$2$$$: the optimal partition is $$$[0, -2, 3]$$$, $$$[-4]$$$, and the sum of values is $$$3+(-1)=2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1667B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1667/problem/B"}